Recommends: fonts-noto-color-emoji
Description: multilingual clipboard and character picker for GNOME Shell
 Super V Ubuntu adds a Windows-style Super+V shell popup with searchable
 clipboard history, emoji, kaomoji, symbols and local GIF favorites.
 Seven interface languages and localized emoji search are bundled. It uses
 GNOME's Wayland clipboard and virtual keyboard APIs without a daemon.
 Users must enable the extension in their own GNOME session. Desktop
 runtime validation is pending; automated logic and package tests exist.
